In this chapter we introduce the subcommands found under [[nytid hr]],
it's the [[cli.hr]] module.
They compute employment data from the completed sign-up sheets:
amanuensis contracts, time sheets, hour summaries and the tracking of
who is reported to HR as employed.

Deferring costs is a theme in this module: the Canvas and LADOK
sessions below are already created lazily by [[get_canvas_session]]
and [[get_ladok_session]], because most invocations never talk to
either service.
The same reasoning applies to the module's own dependencies.
The CLI loads every subcommand module at start-up, and top-level
imports of [[nytid.signup.hr]], [[nytid.signup.sheets]] and
[[nytid.signup.hr.timesheet]]---the last dragging in [[openpyxl]]
and PIL---cost about 70\,ms on every nytid invocation.
We therefore import them inside the functions that use them,
module-style ([[from nytid.signup import hr]]), so that tests
patching attributes on the source modules still take effect at call
time.
The module-scope code---config-key constants and option
defaults---uses none of them, and the names imported from
[[signupsheets]] stay at the top since that module keeps its own
heavy imports function-local.
