\subsection{Naming the planning spreadsheet}
\label{sec:xlsx-format}

The planning spreadsheet is handed to someone else, and that someone
decides what the file should be called.
Our own habit is to name it after the TA's username and the time of
generation, so repeated runs never clobber each other and the files sort
chronologically.
The TCS department instead wants
[[AmanuensensFörnamn_AmanuensensEfternamn_kortkodkursKursomgång_period]],
for instance [[Emma_Riese_prgwv26_P4.xlsx]].
Those two conventions are incompatible, and there will be others, so the
naming is a named \emph{format} the user picks rather than something we
hardcode.

We would have liked [[--xlsx]] itself to take the format as an optional
value, so that a bare [[--xlsx]] keeps its old meaning while
[[--xlsx TCS]] selects the new one.
Click supports exactly that ([[is_flag=False]] with a [[flag_value]]),
but Typer rejects those parameters, so an option cannot be both a bare
flag and take a value.
We therefore keep [[--xlsx]] as the switch that turns the export on and
add [[--xlsx-format]] to choose the naming.
The default is the [[username]] format, so existing invocations behave
exactly as before, and since a department's convention rarely changes
the default can be set once in the configuration.
<<option [[xlsx]] to export the planning spreadsheet>>=
xlsx: Annotated[bool, xlsx_opt] = False,
xlsx_format: Annotated[XlsxFormat, xlsx_format_opt] = DEFAULT_XLSX_FORMAT
