\subsection{Test fixture for the employment store}

The CLI tests need both stores configured: the coverage check in
[[missing]] and [[report]] reads the contract store too, and letting
that lookup fall back to the working directory would make the tests
sensitive to whatever JSON files happen to be there.
So the fixture serves both config keys, each backed by its own
temporary directory, the contract one empty.
<<test setup>>=
@pytest.fixture
def temp_employment_dir(monkeypatch):
  """Creates temporary employment record and contract stores."""
  with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as empdir, \
       tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as contractsdir:
    employment_path = pathlib.Path(empdir)

    def mock_config_get(key):
      if key == "hr.employment.employment_dir":
        return str(employment_path)
      if key == "hr.amanuensis.contract_dir":
        return str(contractsdir)
      raise KeyError(f"Config key {key} not found")

    import typerconf
    monkeypatch.setattr(typerconf, "get", mock_config_get)

    yield employment_path
